bic_trace_step.reason:
This commit introduces the `log->l_iclog_roundoff` field in `xlog_alloc_log` and sets it to `BBSIZE` (512 bytes) in the `else` branch when the superblock lacks a log stripe unit: 

+ if (xfs_sb_version_haslogv2(&mp->m_sb) && mp->m_sb.sb_logsunit > 1)
+ log->l_iclog_roundoff = mp->m_sb.sb_logsunit;
+ else
+ log->l_iclog_roundoff = BBSIZE;

This fails to account for larger log sector sizes (`mp->m_sb.sb_logsectsize`), which is the exact root cause of the vulnerability.
